<title>ITALY: FORECAST - Italy implied rates signal cheaper money.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - Italy implied rates signal cheaper money.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian implicit forward rates point to an easing of short and medium term interest rates, according to a weekly forecast by Milan's Bocconi university.</p>
<p>Implicit forward rates, worked out by extrapolating from existing fixed term market rates, suggest not only a cut in the central bank's 6.75 percent discount rate in the short term but also a lasting fall in market rates, according to the survey.</p>
<p>The market is looking for an overnight rate below seven percent within a month and even lower in three months time.</p>
<p>The overnight rate is forecast at 6.95 percent within a month against 7.07 percent in last week's forcast. The overnight rate stood at 7.13 percent on the interbank market on Thursday, the day on which the forecast is based.</p>
<p>On a three-month time horizon, the overnight rate is seen falling to 6.70 percent, down from 6.92 percent in last week's forecast and compared with 7.03 percent in a survey one month ago.</p>
<p>The overnight rate is seen falling further to 6.44 percent in a year's time, down from 6.73 percent over the same period in last week's forecast and 6.77 percent in the forecast one month ago.</p>
